project: product
component: Tooling
kind: Fixed
body: >
  Tighten CP00-PROOF-LEVEL-CONTRADICTION word-boundary rules so that a
  proof-level term (`release`, `public`, `installed`, `packaged`,
  `presentation`) embedded only as part of a hyphenated or
  `_`-separated compound identifier (`source-release`, `source_release`,
  `source_public_release`, `installed_proof_requirement`) does not
  donate that term to a contradiction reading. This eliminates the
  false positive on #15504 where an Acceptance bullet naming
  `source-release` and a PR body discussing `any release in common`
  were read as contradictory even though no proof level was required.
time: 2026-09-15T16:45:00Z
custom:
  PR: "15505"
  Slug: cp00-proof-level-hyphenated-compound
  Breaking: "no"
